 "audit": {
  "axes": "pipeline Cartesian x = a = 3.31 A = zigzag, y = b = out of plane, z = c = 4.37 A = armchair; (h00) -> U_xx = U11, (00l) -> U_zz = U33, identical to Z20",
  "labels": "pipeline: Setyawan-Curtarolo (ASE) labels, X = (0.55 a*,0,0) zigzag, Z = (0,0,c*/2) armchair, A = corner. S21 text: Gamma-X is armchair, Gamma-A is zigzag. The two conventions differ; matched by coordinates. (reference_measurements.md reads the S21 Fig. 2b inset as the opposite assignment; the S21 text, quoted in the module docstring, is used here.)",
  "msd_definition": "per-atom <u_a u_b> = hbar/(2 M N) sum (2n+1)/omega Re(e_a e_b*), projected on G-hat; I/I0 = exp(-G.dU.G) as Z20 Eqs. 2-3. Cross-check with phonopy thermal displacements: U_xx/U_yy/U_zz(100 K) = 3.19/4.55/4.74 e-3 A^2 (phonopy, same grid) vs 3.36/4.33/4.85 e-3 (pipeline); converged 24x24x18 grid: 3.24/4.71/4.92 e-3; dU(100->304 K) = 3.83/6.50/6.89 e-3 (phonopy, thermal) vs pipeline at 100 ps 3.87/6.29/7.38 e-3. No bookkeeping error.",
  "equilibrium": "harmonic MACE: dU(100->370 K) = 5.2e-3 (zigzag), 9.4e-3 (armchair) A^2 from phonopy thermal displacements; the measured asymptotic dMSD (1.53e-3, 2.50e-3) is 3.4-3.8x smaller than a fully thermal lattice at the experiment's own dT = 270 K. In the classical limit dU/dT = 3 hbar^2/(M k Theta^2) for a Debye solid; the measured slopes imply Theta_eff ~ 900 K (zigzag) and ~710 K (armchair), the MACE phonons 490 K and 370 K.",
  "verdict": "no convention or bookkeeping bug in run_material.py; the diffuse-point labels differ between conventions and are matched by coordinates; the amplitude excess is a physics/measurement question, not fixed here"
 },
